love.resize <#resize>

Called when the window is resized, for example if the user resizes the
window, or if love.window.setMode <#window_setMode> is called with an
unsupported width or height in fullscreen and the window chooses the
closest appropriate size.

love.resize( w, h )

w	number	The new width.
h	number	The new height.

love.run <#run>

The main function, containing the main loop. A sensible default is used
when left out.

mainLoop = love.run()

